        /* v34.16 FIX (Galaxy on Fire): M3G 1.1 single-arg VOID form
         * bindTarget(Object) — Fishlabs' Abyss wrapper (class s.a(Graphics))
         * calls exactly this descriptor. Without it bindTarget was a silent
         * no-op: g_m3g_bindtarget_called stayed false, every render(Node,Transform)
         * went into the pending queue (64) and then fell through to immediate
         * rendering with an uninitialized vertex pool (capacity 0 — the pool
         * is only initialized inside m3g_context_init, which only bindTarget
         * and force-render call) — ALL meshes were dropped ("vertex pool
         * exhausted: need N, have 0"). The 3arg handler ignores its extra
         * args (never reads args[2]/args[3]) and the void-descriptor call
         * site discards the returned object (dispatcher pushes results only
         * for non-void return descriptors), so it is directly reusable. */
